  "verification": "V10 requires exact installed-byte native entry, hold, escalation, and recovery tests with hard below, equal to, and above soft; automatic and native-ceiling behavior; inactive/ignition parity; and configured V7/V8/V9 upgrade/removal preservation. V8 arming and speed/TPS release bytes remain unchanged. Vehicle validation remains required.",
  "title": "Launch Control / 2-step",
  "user_description": "Adds launch control using native staged fuel cut or shared ignition cut. Fuel hard RPM may be below soft RPM; native RPM ceilings remain effective. Always mode still respects arming speed, maximum speed, and minimum throttle.",
  "description": "MS41.1 Launch Control V10. E847.1 is the launch-only spark-cut request, E847.2 records actual native launch fuel cut, and the launch-arm latch uses IRAM FDB6.6, certified free on the canonical 1437806 image. Vehicle speed reads F1BE. LC_HYST is RPM/32 (FF means zero hysteresis), and LC_IPW is uint16 x0.00534 ms (FFFF preserves stock injection); both apply only to launch ignition mode. Ignition mode never clears standalone E847.0, and LC_IPW wins while both spark requests are active. Fuel mode retains the native staged limiter and caps the independent explicit or automatic launch hard threshold at native hard RPM. A lower explicit launch hard setting also lowers the native soft/recovery anchor, preserving native fuel hysteresis and countdown behavior without allowing the limiter to clear above the lower hard setting. Always mode acts as an asserted input only after the shared speed and throttle gates; it cannot rearm at or above LC_ARMSPEED.",
